  "heading": "\\set.successor:of{X}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{The set successor of }X\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{X \\cup \\left \\{ X \\right \\}}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\set.successor:of{X}]\nDefines: Y is \\set\nwhen: X is \\set\nexpresses:\n. let: Z is \\set\n  then:\n  . have: Z \"in\"? Y\n    iff:\n    . (.Z = X.) \\.or./ (.Z = \\set.singleton.set:of{X}.)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"The set successor of $X?$\"\n. written: \"X? \\cup \\left \\{ X? \\right \\}\"\n. description: \"The successor of $X$ is the set $X \\cup \\{X\\}$, whose members\n                are the members of $X$ together with $X$ itself. Starting from\n                $\\emptyset$ and repeating this step generates the natural\n                numbers.\"\nId: \"002b9914-ad06-4f5a-a3fb-803bd86e6c4b\"",
